    {
      "text": "Marowak is the evolved form of a Cubone that has overcome its sadness at the loss of its mother and grown tough. This Pokémon’s tempered and hardened spirit is not easily broken.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Originally, it was weak and timid. After evolution, its temperament becomes violent, and it begins to wield bones as weapons.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is out for vengeance on its natural enemy, Mandibuzz. It throws bones like boomerangs to try to take it down.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It throws bones at Mandibuzz to knock it down. It’s thought that Marowak is trying to avenge its parent.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "They thump their bones rhythmically to communicate among themselves. There are nearly 50 different rhythmic patterns.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Small and weak, this Pokémon is adept with its bone club. It has grown more vicious over the ages.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Small and weak, this Pokémon is adept with its bone club. It has grown more vicious over the ages.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon overcame its sorrow to evolve a sturdy new body. Marowak faces its opponents bravely, using a bone as a weapon.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "When this Pokémon evolved, the skull of its mother fused to it. Marowak’s temperament also turned vicious at the same time.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
